.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt DSCL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dscl
.Nd read and change directory records
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl plist
.Ar node
.Fl read
.Ar path
.Op Ar key ...
.Nm
.Op Fl plist
.Ar node
.Fl list
.Ar path
.Op Ar key
.Nm
.Ar node
.Fl create
.Ar path
.Op Ar key Op Ar value ...
.Nm
.Ar node
.Fl append
.Ar path key value ...
.Nm
.Ar node
.Fl delete
.Ar path
.Op Ar key Op Ar value ...
.Nm
.Ar node
.Fl passwd
.Ar path
.Op Ar new_password | old_password new_password
.Nm
.Fl f Ar dir
.Fl create | append | delete | passwd
.Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes the records that
.Xr opendirectoryd 8
keeps.
The daemon decides who may change what.
.Pp
With
.Fl f ,
.Nm
changes the records in the dslocal node directory
.Ar dir ,
such as
.Pa /var/db/dslocal/nodes/Default
on another volume, without the daemon, with the caller's rights.
It takes the
.Fl create ,
.Fl append ,
.Fl delete
and
.Fl passwd
commands.
.Fl passwd
without a password asks for it twice on the terminal, or reads one line
from the standard input if that is not a terminal.
.Pp
.Ar node
is a node name, such as
.Pa /Local/Default
or
.Pa /Search .
A dot or
.Li localhost
means
.Pa /Local/Default .
.Ar path
is
.Pa / Ns Ar type Ns Pa / Ns Ar name ,
such as
.Pa /Users/pie
or
.Pa /Groups/admin ,
or
.Pa / Ns Ar type
for
.Fl list .
.Ar key
is an attribute name.
A standard name may be given without its
.Li dsAttrTypeStandard:
prefix.
Any other name without a prefix is taken as
.Li dsAttrTypeNative: Ns Ar key .
The commands may also be given without their dash.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl read Ar path Op Ar key ...
Print the record's attributes, or only the keys given, one per line
in the form
.Ar key Ns : Ar values .
Standard names are printed without their prefix.
If a value is empty or holds a space, each value goes on a line of its
own, after a space.
Data is printed in hex.
.It Fl list Ar path Op Ar key
Print the names of the records of a type, sorted, with the values of
.Ar key
after each name.
.Fl list Pa /
prints the record types.
.It Fl create Ar path Op Ar key Op Ar value ...
Create the record if it does not exist.
With a key, set the attribute to the values given, replacing any it has,
or to one empty value.
A new user gets a GeneratedUID and a random password.
.It Fl append Ar path key value ...
Add the values to the attribute.
.It Fl delete Ar path Op Ar key Op Ar value ...
Delete the record, the attribute or the values given.
.It Fl passwd Ar path Op Ar new_password | old_password new_password
Set a user's password.
With no password given,
.Nm
asks for the old one, unless run by root, and for the new one twice.
Passwords on the command line are visible to other users.
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl plist ,
.Fl read
and
.Fl list
print an XML property list, with the full attribute names.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success, 1 on an error and 2 on a usage error.
.Fl read
also exits 1 when a key it was asked for is missing.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show a user:
.Dl dscl . -read /Users/pie
.Pp
List the users with their numbers:
.Dl dscl . -list /Users UniqueID
.Pp
As root, add a user and make them an administrator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dscl . -create /Users/ann
dscl . -create /Users/ann UniqueID 502
dscl . -create /Users/ann PrimaryGroupID 20
dscl . -create /Users/ann NFSHomeDirectory /Users/ann
dscl . -create /Users/ann UserShell /bin/sh
dscl . -create /Users/ann RealName "Ann Example"
dscl . -passwd /Users/ann
dscl . -append /Groups/admin GroupMembership ann
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr opendirectoryd 8
.Sh BUGS
There is no interactive mode, and no way to give credentials for a node.
